    title: "Iraqi PM Ali al-Zaidi meets Ahmed al-Sharaa in historic Syria visit",
    summary: "Talks focused on enhancing trade, reviving Baniyas oil pipeline and achieving stability through cooperation.",
    preview: "Iraqi Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi has arrived in Damascus to meet with Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa on the first visit of an Iraqi prime minister to Syria since the fall of Bashar al-Assad. The visit comes as the two neighbours seek to strengthen bilateral ties and boost economic and oil cooperation. Recommended Stories list of 3 items - list 1 of 3Why Jordan has struck Syria: What we know - list 2 of 3Syria-Jordan border reopens amid probe into deadly air strikes - list 3 of 3Victims of Jordan’s air strikes in Syria According to the official Iraqi…",
    body: "Iraqi Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi has arrived in Damascus to meet with Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa on the first visit of an Iraqi prime minister to Syria since the fall of Bashar al-Assad.\n\nThe visit comes as the two neighbours seek to strengthen bilateral ties and boost economic and oil cooperation.\n\nRecommended Stories\n\nlist of 3 items\n\n- list 1 of 3Why Jordan has struck Syria: What we know\n\n- list 2 of 3Syria-Jordan border reopens amid probe into deadly air strikes\n\n- list 3 of 3Victims of Jordan’s air strikes in Syria\n\nAccording to the official Iraqi News Agency (INA), the two leaders discussed the export of Iraqi oil through the Baniyas line, increasing the volume of trade exchange and joint work to develop the agricultural sector to achieve food and economic integration.\n\nIraq has recently begun exporting limited quantities of oil through Syria following the outbreak of the US-led war on Iran.\n\nLast July, the two countries signed agreements to revive the Haditha Baniyas pipeline to transport Iraqi oil in addition to signing a memorandum of understanding with a consortium of three companies, most notably the American oil major Chevron to implement the project.\n\n“The Iraqi and Syrian people are one people in two countries,” Zaidi said according to INA, noting that “work to develop partnership and joint cooperation in various fields especially economic and social affairs, enhance security co-operation, unify positions on regional and international issues, and work to achieve peace and stability in the region”.\n\nFor his part, the Syrian president expressed his “great appreciation for the visit of al-Zaidi and his accompanying delegation,” stressing “the depth of bilateral relations and Syria’s keenness to achieve the highest levels of cooperation between the two countries”.\n\nAl-Sharaa and al-Zaidi had previously met last September in New York on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, where they discussed ways to strengthen political and security coordination and expand economic and trade cooperation.",
